Write a function `stream(SpeechPrompt speechPrompt)` that takes a speech prompt containing text and synthesis options, converts it into a speech request using a helper method `createRequest`, calls an API to generate speech, and returns a Flux of SpeechResponse objects where each response contains the audio data. You should write self-contained code starting with: ```java
@Override
public Flux<SpeechResponse> stream(SpeechPrompt speechPrompt) {
}```

solutions.solution:
@Override
public Flux<SpeechResponse> stream(SpeechPrompt speechPrompt) {
	OpenAiAudioApi.SpeechRequest speechRequest = createRequest(speechPrompt);

	return this.audioApi.stream(speechRequest)
		.map(responseEntity -> {
			var speech = responseEntity.getBody();

			if (speech == null) {
				logger.warn("No speech response returned for speechRequest: {}", speechRequest);
				return new SpeechResponse(new Speech(new byte[0]));
			}

			RateLimit rateLimits = OpenAiResponseHeaderExtractor.extractAiResponseHeaders(responseEntity);

			return new SpeechResponse(new Speech(speech), new OpenAiAudioSpeechResponseMetadata(rateLimits));
		});
}

